==Notes==
* Although shouts need to be spoken for their power to manifest, dragons seem to only roar when using most shouts.
* Outside of the main quest, the most reliable way to find dragons to fight is to perform the radiant quests [[Skyrim:Dragon Seekers|Dragon Seekers]] or [[Skyrim:Dragon Hunting|Dragon Hunting]]. They are repeatable, and your destination is guaranteed to spawn a dragon. [[Skyrim:Dragon Seekers|Dragon Seekers]] is available if you have completed the [[Skyrim:Companions|Companions]] questline and [[Skyrim:Dragon Rising|Dragon Rising]], and [[Skyrim:Dragon Hunting|Dragon Hunting]] is available if you have completed [[Skyrim:Rebuilding the Blades|Rebuilding the Blades]] and are on friendly terms with the Blades.
* While [[Skyrim:A Blade in the Dark|A Blade in the Dark]] is active, dragon locations will be limited to dragon lairs, and random dragon encounters are disabled.
*Although [[Skyrim:Arngeir|Arngeir]] says that dragons have the same ability as the [[Skyrim:Dovahkiin|Dovahkiin]] to absorb a slain dragon's soul, receive its knowledge, and use this to master a new shout, it never happens during gameplay. This is presumably because there is no occasion when one dragon fights or kills another, unless you have summoned or mastered one: and on such an occasion, you are present to absorb the dragon soul, whether you want or need it or not.
**He does, however, say that dragons have always been able to shout since the dawn of time, a dragon's ability to shout in the Dragon Language is intrinsic to their very being, and the latter comes naturally to them as breathing or speaking.
*If you instantly kill a dragon while it rests on a word wall, or is completing an animation such as taking flight, the dragon will finish its animation (it will take flight if it is resting), before landing (or crashing) to die. This is due to the longer animation sequences associated with dragons due to their size.
*Legendary Dragons will occasionally seem to taunt you by announcing their presence before attacking. {{vn|section=Legendary_Dragons_taunting_player}}
*The [[Skyrim:Wabbajack|Wabbajack]] will not transform a dragon, but can be used as a constant source of destructive blasts.
*If ''[[Skyrim:Dragonborn|Dragonborn]]'' is installed and the quest [[Skyrim:The Temple of Miraak|The Temple of Miraak]] has been completed though the quest [[Skyrim:At the Summit of Apocrypha|At the Summit of Apocrypha]] has not been finished, [[Skyrim:Miraak (person)|Miraak]] may appear and absorb the dragon soul before you can. He will always appear for the first dragon you defeat and will have a 25% chance to appear after that. He can appear on Solstheim, and in Skyrim as well.
*Dragon's souls cannot be [[Skyrim:Soul Trap (effect)|trapped]]; only consumed.
*Dragons are immune to all [[Skyrim:Illusion|Illusion]] spells and effects cast at them.
*Dragons have extremely high [[Skyrim:Sneak|Sneak]] ability, which allows them to significantly counter most forms of stealth, including invisibility and muffle, though they're not technically immune to these effects, meaning it is still possible to sneak around a dragon, just much harder than normal.
*Revered and Legendary dragons use Durnehviir's voice when using the Drain Vitality shout.

==Bugs==
[[File:SR-creature-Dragon LOD Bug.jpg|thumb|right|A dragon with the LOD texture bug]]
{{Bug|You will occasionally fail to absorb a dragon's soul after killing one. This issue can possibly result from fast traveling, mounting a horse, looting a container, or engaging an NPC in dialogue the moment the dragon dies.|confirmed=1|USKP|1.0}}
**{{Pc22}} A workaround is to use a console command: <code>player.modav dragonsouls 1</code>
**This bug usually occurs with dragons that have spawned from [[Skyrim:Dragon Lairs|dragon lairs]] after you first visit them.
{{Bug|Dragons and draugr are considered enemies, even though dragon priests are allies to both.|USKP|1.2|fixdetail=Dragons and draugr are no longer hostile to one another.}}
{{Bug|There is a missing level 27 fire dragon in the leveled list lchardragonany even though they exist and should have been ON the list at level 27 since all other levels have them.|USKP|2.1.2}}
{{Bug|The level 27 fire dragon mentioned above is also absent from the leveled list dlc2lchardragonany even though they exist and also should have been on the list at level 27 for the same reason.|UDBP|2.1.2}}
{{Bug|The 3rd tier fire dragon is incorrectly based on a 4th tier template which causes them to spawn as level 40 rather than the correct level 30 they should be.|USLEEP|3.0.1}}
{{Bug|Dragons may be capable of reporting [[Skyrim:Crime|crimes]] against you.|USSEP|4.3.7}}
{{Bug|Dragons will occasionally lunge through cover such as boulders, sarcophagi, and trees.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|If you have the [[Skyrim:Disintegrate|Disintegrate]] perk and you disintegrate a dragon with a Shock spell, the ashes may disappear into the world terrain (or just be very hard to find). You will still absorb the dragon soul, but will miss out on the dragon bones and scales as well as the other leveled loot.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|If there are no open spaces nearby, wounded dragons (or those under the effects of Dragonrend) will sometimes be forced to crash-land and skid through solid objects, and often teleport wildly and/or end up at odd angles.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|Casting most spells on a dead dragon's skeleton may move it incredible distances.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|Right after a dragon dies, you can walk inside its corpse and view its skeleton before it disintegrates.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|Dragons may fly improperly through objects after you exit an interior.|OSP|1.1}}
{{Bug|Dragons may not properly give you their souls upon death. Dragon corpses also may not clean up properly.|OSP|1.2}}
{{Bug|You may see some dragons flying backwards. These dragons are not affected by Dragonrend and never land, so they can only be killed by arrows and spells. This bug was introduced with Patch 1.2.|confirmed=1|OSP|1.3}}
{{Bug|Dragon landings can occasionally cause the game to crash.|OSP|1.7}}
{{Bug|After [[Skyrim:Dragonslayer|Dragonslayer]] is finished, the instance of random dragon attacks after fast traveling is supposed to be reduced, but isn't.|OSP|1.9}}
{{Bug|During [[Skyrim:Battle for Whiterun|Battle for Whiterun]], a dragon may attack the city, complicating matters even further.|OSP|1.9}}
{{Bug|Miraak may sometimes not be present if he steals dragon souls.|OSSEP|1.6.1130}}
{{Bug|Sometimes after leaving a building or fast traveling, dragon skeletons will spawn and fall from the sky, without you fighting them at all.|confirmed=1}}
**In some cases this is a result of the way the game saves data. When returning to an area where a dragon has been killed, after the cell has been unloaded from the buffer but before the corpse would have expired, the corpse is respawned in the air (as if a live dragon) and allowed to fall again.
{{Bug|Dragons may spawn with their distant skin model instead of their close-up model, and will appear blocky with blurred skin.|confirmed=1}}
**Saving and reloading will correct this.
{{Bug|On the PC, some have experienced a glitch when performing one-handed weapon "finishing moves" on dragons in which the animation will be off-center. In most cases, it will appear as though the character is dangling off the right side of the dragon's head when the finisher animation occurs.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|Dragons can occasionally become invisible for no apparent reason, although NPCs will still attack them.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|When you visit a dragon lair, the dragon may be in front of the word wall stuck in the ground. This renders the dragon unkillable and it will not attack you.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|Using [[Skyrim:Storm Call|Storm Call]] to kill a dragon that's still flying may make it continuously fly in circles and become unkillable.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|If you fast travel after killing a flying dragon, the dragon may appear in that area.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|Sometimes dragons are unlootable.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|Dragons landing on stairs can get stuck since each step is its own surface and they cannot fit on a single step. This causes them to be stuck until the forced landing sequence, and in this case they simply jump up and crash back down.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|On rare occasions, a dragon soul will be absorbed before the dragon is dead, leaving an invulnerable skeletal dragon.|section=Soul absorbtion from alive dragon|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug|Sometimes, a dragon may get stuck in a circle flight and will be unable to land or hover. They also become immune to Dragonrend, you can see the shout effect hitting them, but they won't land. They can only be killed by arrows or spells, and in some cases they will continue to fly in circles after their health is reduced to 0.|confirmed=1}}
**Entering a building and going back outside fixes this.
**{{Pc22}} Select the dragon in the [[Skyrim:Console|console]] and then type <code>evp</code>. The dragon will usually break out of the loop and land, but it can take a couple of tries sometimes.
{{Bug| When the game tries to reload a dragon corpse that was previously unloaded it may fail to do so correctly and end up dropping the corpse in a default location as a fail-safe, which is usually somewhere near you. The corpse will then proceed to reload in whatever default location it can find as you move to other areas. This can lead to dragon corpses spawning in odd places such as in front of [[Skyrim:Dragonsreach|Dragonsreach]] without any apparent explanation.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug| When you visit a Dragon Lair, the dragon may not attack you or become aggressive unless you attack them first.|confirmed=1}}
{{Bug| If you apply magicka draining effects such as Sparks to a dragon as it shouts, and the dragon runs out of magicka mid-shout, it will fail to shout and will continue to fail until you stop draining it. Despite this, dragons who have no magicka are still able to shout, as long as magicka is not being actively drained from them. This is likely due to a Combat AI bug, as shouts do not consume magicka.|confirmed=1}}

